{"authored" [{"question" "q-162150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/assets/e2ab6906100a96a123b4b1520613f1e38fe2c7e77af390a8efe0596a2861727d.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/state.json" "file_sha256" "827e2d0c67871315f13e9696a969ecd768ed6615275885cde1daeb05656b49d3" "basis" 1435 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Recall that for any linear transformation $T$ with associated $2\\times 2$ matrix $T,$ we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., $det(T)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., $det(T)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $T$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $T$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is the point $(0,0),$ the origin of the coordinate system.\n\nSince $T$ is the zero matrix, the image of our object under the action of $T$ is the origin." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/state.json" "file_sha256" "827e2d0c67871315f13e9696a969ecd768ed6615275885cde1daeb05656b49d3" "basis" 1435 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162150" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "06739ce6498263f9c042f447fdb5e02ed1b51689c86067f26597e2e4e241dcd8" "basis" 1435 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/state.json" "file_sha256" "827e2d0c67871315f13e9696a969ecd768ed6615275885cde1daeb05656b49d3" "basis" 1435 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A line segment"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/state.json" "file_sha256" "827e2d0c67871315f13e9696a969ecd768ed6615275885cde1daeb05656b49d3" "basis" 1435 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A point, different from the origin"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/state.json" "file_sha256" "827e2d0c67871315f13e9696a969ecd768ed6615275885cde1daeb05656b49d3" "basis" 1435 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A rectangle"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/state.json" "file_sha256" "827e2d0c67871315f13e9696a969ecd768ed6615275885cde1daeb05656b49d3" "basis" 1435 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "A triangle"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/state.json" "file_sha256" "827e2d0c67871315f13e9696a969ecd768ed6615275885cde1daeb05656b49d3" "basis" 1435 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-162150" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/text "The origin $O$ of the coordinate system"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/state.json" "file_sha256" "827e2d0c67871315f13e9696a969ecd768ed6615275885cde1daeb05656b49d3" "basis" 1435 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040372/edb-import/verification.json"}] "sources" [{"question" "q-96873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/131d9f30fac5b1cc4b8eb72a989ca16b0d3cbf7d16725aa38581bfd115b1fc77.png)\n\nConsider the linear transformation $T$ with matrix representation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nWhich of the following is the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb2aa274fc22a823f7da17bbc9877c568f92c7bf9552f6f68f62869d3e322f1d"} {"question" "q-96873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To find the image of the triangle under the action of $T$, we first create a matrix $X$ containing all of the vertices of the triangle:\n\n$$\nX=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nNow, we compute the image of $X$ under the action of $T$ by calculating the matrix product $TX:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}TX & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & -4 \\\\ -2 & 2 & 8\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the image's vertices are $(1,-2)$, $(-1,2),$ $(-4,8).$ Notice that all three points lie on the same line.\n\nSo, the image of our triangle under the action of $T$ is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/assets/87d2a7f522d68e1a50d9c5bb5e33498b2a28e869785f5109c4f6bf3a1c7ff701.png)" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/state.json" "file_sha256" "eb2aa274fc22a823f7da17bbc9877c568f92c7bf9552f6f68f62869d3e322f1d"} {"question" "q-96873" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14060375/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "6293cc96a6d4aa4d9688bc8a6add7d10e203b0bfe03b78c08ef4c2c0c4a